 three points, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters, and prediction markets price his win odds in the low 60s. Husted's incumbency and Ohio's Republican-leaning electorate keep the race short of Likely Democratic.", "watch": "A late wave of Republican spending and turnout mobilized by Trump's visits could close the low-single-digit gap in the final week.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Husted (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's special Senate election pits appointed Republican incumbent Jon Husted against Sherrod Brown, the Democrat who held the seat for 18 years before losing it in 2022. Polling across more than a dozen October surveys shows Brown ahead by roughly three to four points on average, with even Republican-sponsored polls showing him tied or better. Independent raters split between Tossup and Lean Democratic, and prediction markets give Brown about a 62 percent chance of winning.\n\nBrown holds a clear money advantage, outraising Husted about two-to-one overall and nearly five-to-one in the final reports, fueling heavy advertising in an expensive media state. Husted counters with the state's Republican lean, the powers of incumbency, and national backing, including a Trump visit to energize the base. A strong Republican turnout operation remains the main obstacle to Brown's return; the race is genuinely competitive but tilts to the Democrat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6851, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7568, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7432, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7463, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2